& [CoreConclusion] is strongly supported
  + the proposal gives Weaver and Planner an implementable shared waist by separating an identity-oriented view from an operation-oriented view
  + IdentityCatalogue answers what bounded subjects exist, what they mean, why they matter, how they relate, and where their authority is sourced
  + OperationCatalogue answers what may be related, observed, inferred, transformed, controlled, or effected, with exact applicability and constraints
  + Weaver instantiates candidate bindings between operation roles and identities
  + Planner searches ordered transitions through those candidates toward an ObjectiveContract
  = concise: identities provide state, operations provide possible transitions, Weaver forms the candidate transition graph, and Planner searches it

& [AuthorityBoundary] keeps both catalogues derived
  + authoritative meaning remains in signed admitted SOP files, semantic units, contracts, relations, and packages
  + IdentityCatalogue and OperationCatalogue are compiled signed projections with exact source anchors and generation roots
  + catalogue entries cannot add meaning, authority, applicability, constraints, or effects absent from governing SOP authority
  + every source or package change requires catalogue regeneration and startup re-attestation before use
  + human-readable table-of-contents and index files are inspectable views of the same compiled records
  - never: let a stale catalogue become a second source of truth

& [IdentityCatalogue] is the table-of-contents projection
  + [catalogue_id], [profile], [version], and [generation_root] are immutable
  + [identity_entries] are sorted by stable identity rather than display spelling
  + [name_index] maps preferred names, proper nouns, aliases, abbreviations, and lexical forms to candidate stable identities
  + [kind] distinguishes entity, concept, role, proposition, contract, file, program, faculty, resource, state, observation, result, and other admitted identity families
  + [description] and [meaning] preserve human summary and exact semantic definition separately
  + [purpose_set] and [use_case_set] state intended relevance without granting universal applicability
  + [context_and_boundary_set] preserve domain, perspective, assumptions, inclusion, exclusion, uncertainty, and identity invariants
  + [relation_refs] preserve typed graph relationships without merging endpoints
  + [source_anchor_set] binds package, file, clause, byte span, digest, and display location
  + [authority_and_lifecycle] preserve scope, signer, certificate, status, version, supersession, staleness, and revocation
  - never: restrict identity to proper nouns because common concepts, roles, propositions, contracts, and states are also addressable subjects

& [OperationCatalogue] is the semantic index projection
  + [catalogue_id], [profile], [version], and [generation_root] are immutable
  + [operation_entries] are sorted by stable operation identity rather than verb spelling
  + [verb_index] maps verbs, aliases, inflections, phrases, and SAIL operation names to candidate operation identities
  + [operation_class] distinguishes relation, observation, query, inference, transformation, validation, control, capability, and physical effect
  + [meaning] defines the operation independently of any one invocation
  + [role_signature] names required subject, object, context, instrument, authority, evidence, and output roles
  + [input_type_constraints] and [output_type_constraints] bind admissible identity kinds and schemas
  + [preconditions], [invariants], [postconditions], and [failure_conditions] define transition semantics
  + [authority_requirements], [effect_class], [reversibility], [risk], [cost], [resource_budget], and [time_horizon] constrain use
  + [non_transfer_set] prevents applicability from transferring identity, evidence, authority, or properties not licensed by the operation
  + [source_anchor_set], [certificate], and [lifecycle] bind exact SOP authority
  - never: make verb presence imply executable capability or effect authority

& [OperationMeaningDelineation] prevents grammar from collapsing semantics
  + [relation] describes a typed connection and may be symmetric, directional, static, or contextual without causing change
  + [observation] produces evidence claims without changing the observed subject by semantic declaration alone
  + [inference] derives a candidate proposition under an inference regime without asserting external effect
  + [transformation] proposes a before-to-after semantic or state delta
  + [control] changes attention, evaluation, or workflow disposition within declared authority
  + [capability] identifies an available mechanism but does not authorize invocation
  + [physical_effect] requires separate EffectBroker authorization and receipt
  = must: preserve these classes even when natural language uses the same verb for several

& [ApplicabilityBinding] is the typed seam between catalogues
  + [binding_id] is immutable
  + [operation_ref] identifies one OperationCatalogue entry
  + [role_ref] identifies the exact operation role being filled
  + [identity_ref_or_type] identifies an exact identity or admissible identity class
  + [context], [purpose], [conditions], and [boundary_refs] state where the binding can hold
  + [evidence_refs] state why applicability is declared or inferred
  + [authority_ref] is required when applicability includes privileged access or effect
  + [transfer_law] and [non_transfer_set] preserve property boundaries
  + [status] is declared, derived, candidate, contradicted, blocked, stale, or unresolved
  + [correlation_score] may rank candidate inspection but cannot change status or authorize traversal

& [ObjectiveContract] makes planning target identity explicit
  + [objective_id] is immutable
  + [subject_refs] identify the starting identities
  + [current_state_ref] identifies admitted entry state
  + [desired_state_predicates] define the target without representing it as achieved
  + [success_evidence] states how completion can be verified
  + [purpose], [priority], [authority], [scope], [constraints], and [protected_identity_refs] govern relevance and admissibility
  + [prohibited_outcomes] and [effect_boundary] limit optimization
  + [resource_budget], [time_horizon], [stop_conditions], and [fallback] bound search
  + [unknowns] preserve missing identity, operation, evidence, capability, or reachability

& [ScannerDelineation] separates retrieval, weaving, and planning
  + [identity_scan] resolves objective terms into bounded IdentityCatalogue candidates
  + [operation_scan] retrieves operations whose declared role signatures and contexts can accept those identities
  + [exact_join] applies stable identity, type, role, purpose, boundary, and condition constraints deterministically
  + [relational_expansion] traverses allowed typed relations and dependency edges within budget
  + [correlation_proposal] may rank additional identity-operation seams from lexical, graph, embedding, or learned evidence
  + [scanner_output] is an inspectable candidate set with grounds, exclusions, contradictions, ambiguity, and omissions
  + the scanner itself neither admits a binding nor selects a plan
  - never: combine retrieval, correlation, Weaver judgment, Planner search, and Observer selection in one opaque score

& [WeaverBehavior] instantiates the candidate transition graph
  + consume bounded objective identities, applicable operation candidates, identity boundaries, relation evidence, and exclusions
  + bind operation roles to distinct identities without erasing their identities or qualified contexts
  + project possible relations, composites, decompositions, seams, input-output compatibility, and incompatibility
  + emit CandidateOperationInstance records containing operation, role bindings, preconditions, constraints, projected outputs, identity deltas, grounds, and unresolved seams
  + reject or qualify type mismatch, unsupported applicability, illegal transfer, contradictory identity, and missing role
  + never select a candidate as true, authorized, temporally reachable, or executable

& [CandidateOperationInstance] is Weaver's principal return form
  + [instance_id] is immutable and content-addressed
  + [operation_ref] binds one admitted operation definition
  + [role_bindings] bind exact admitted or explicitly candidate identities
  + [applicability_refs] preserve every seam used
  + [precondition_state] is satisfied, unsatisfied, disputed, unavailable, or unresolved
  + [constraint_refs] and [boundary_refs] bind all active limits
  + [projected_output_refs] identify candidate results or after-state predicates
  + [identity_delta] preserves material semantic and operational change
  + [authority_and_effect_requirements] remain ungranted requirements
  + [grounds], [counterevidence], [uncertainty], and [residuals] remain visible

& [PlannerBehavior] searches ordered objective paths
  + consume current state, ObjectiveContract, Weaver candidate instances, prerequisites, dependencies, verification operations, and stop conditions
  + build candidate paths whose steps identify exact before predicates, operation instance, expected after predicates, checks, and failure branches
  + accumulate authority, identity delta, constraints, risk, cost, resources, time, uncertainty, and effect exposure across the whole path
  + distinguish reachable, conditionally reachable, unreachable, blocked, cycle, over-budget, and unresolved branches
  + prefer the smallest checkable path only after preserving all material obligations and alternatives
  + never represent a desired or projected state as achieved and never commit an effect

& [CandidatePlan] is Planner's principal return form
  + [plan_id] is immutable and objective-bound
  + [entry_state_ref] and [objective_ref] preserve endpoints
  + [ordered_step_set] references CandidateOperationInstance values and verification checks
  + [dependency_and_branch_graph] preserves prerequisites, alternatives, failure, rollback, stop, and reroute
  + [cumulative_identity_delta], [constraint_account], [authority_account], [risk_account], [effect_account], and [uncertainty_account] are explicit
  + [completion_evidence_plan] states how success would be observed
  + [status] is candidate, qualified, unreachable, blocked, over_budget, cyclic, or unresolved

& [WeaverPlannerReciprocity] becomes a typed fixed-point search
  + Weaver rejects a Planner path whose steps misuse identity bindings, relation transfer, or operation composition
  + Planner rejects a Weaver composition that lacks reachable prerequisites, verification, ordering, or bounded consequences
  + Weaver may decompose an impossible operation instance into smaller semantic seams
  + Planner may request alternate bindings or operations when a branch is blocked
  + iteration is bounded by graph, path, time, resource, novelty, and no-gain limits
  + convergence means relational and temporal supportability, not truth, admission, or execution

& [GuardAndDisposition] keeps candidate generation subordinate
  + Honesty validates names, meanings, source bindings, applicability claims, assumption status, projected identity deltas, and success evidence
  + Security validates authority, scope, constraints, protected identities, capability use, cumulative effects, containment, and reversibility
  + Refiner selects or expresses the smallest supported candidate delta without removing qualifications
  + Observer decides whether to admit, revise, reroute, decompose, block, or escalate the candidate semantic transition
  + Scribe preserves objective, scans, joins, projections, plans, gates, disposition, and residuals
  + EffectBroker remains the only later path to physical effect commitment

& [ProcessingSequence] is objective-directed
  * bind ObjectiveContract and current state
  * resolve subject and purpose through IdentityCatalogue
  * retrieve role-compatible OperationCatalogue entries
  * exact-join declared ApplicabilityBinding records
  * boundedly propose correlation candidates with explicit grounds
  * Weaver emits CandidateOperationInstance graph
  * Planner emits CandidatePlan paths and cumulative accounts
  * Weaver and Planner cross-review until bounded convergence or no gain
  * Honesty and Security independently gate the candidate
  * Refiner forms the smallest supported next semantic delta
  * Observer disposes and Scribe records
  * any effect remains an uncommitted proposal pending EffectBroker

& [CurrentImplementationFit] is partial and architecturally aligned
  + current SemanticUnit already supports stable identity, kind including Operation, expression, aliases, meaning, context, sources, and status
  + current SemanticRelation and SemanticFabric provide exact and typed graph substrate, but current RelationType is intentionally narrow
  + current query engine already applies exact identity and contextual filtering before relation traversal and lexical retrieval
  + current IdentityBoundary, CombinatoryProjection, Weaver and Planner stages, returns, and ledgers provide constitutional framing
  + current model lacks first-class IdentityCatalogueEntry, OperationSignature, ApplicabilityBinding, ObjectiveContract, CandidateOperationInstance, CandidatePlan, and cumulative path accounts
  + no current scanner performs the complete staged identity-operation-objective behavior described here

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is WPIO-001 through WPIO-020
  + [WPIO-001] define signed derived IdentityCatalogue and human table-of-contents projection
  + [WPIO-002] define signed derived OperationCatalogue and human semantic-index projection
  + [WPIO-003] preserve authoritative meaning in source-anchored admitted SOP rather than either catalogue
  + [WPIO-004] represent preferred names, proper nouns, aliases, kinds, meanings, purposes, contexts, boundaries, relations, sources, authority, and lifecycle for identities
  + [WPIO-005] represent verb aliases, operation classes, role signatures, types, preconditions, invariants, postconditions, failures, authority, effects, risk, reversibility, cost, resources, and source for operations
  + [WPIO-006] distinguish relation, observation, inference, transformation, control, capability, and effect operations
  + [WPIO-007] define ApplicabilityBinding with exact roles, contexts, purpose, evidence, boundaries, authority, transfer law, status, and optional candidate score
  + [WPIO-008] define ObjectiveContract with current state, desired predicates, success evidence, constraints, protected identities, prohibited outcomes, budgets, horizon, stop, fallback, and unknowns
  + [WPIO-009] stage identity scan, operation scan, exact join, relational expansion, and correlation proposal separately
  + [WPIO-010] forbid correlation score from admission, property transfer, authority, or execution
  + [WPIO-011] define Weaver CandidateOperationInstance and preserve role bindings, applicability, preconditions, constraints, outputs, deltas, requirements, evidence, and residuals
  + [WPIO-012] define Planner CandidatePlan with ordered steps, branch graph, cumulative accounts, verification, and closed status
  + [WPIO-013] require bounded Weaver-Planner cross-review and no-gain termination
  + [WPIO-014] require independent Honesty and Security gates before Observer disposition
  + [WPIO-015] preserve Refiner, Scribe, Observer, and EffectBroker delineation
  + [WPIO-016] regenerate, sign, and re-attest catalogue projections on authoritative root change
  + [WPIO-017] preserve exact source anchors and proof for every returned identity, operation, applicability edge, instance, and plan step
  + [WPIO-018] explicitly return excluded, contradictory, stale, unauthorized, unreachable, blocked, clipped, and unresolved material
  + [WPIO-019] test homonymous identity, overloaded verb, wrong role binding, unsupported correlation, authority laundering, constraint accumulation, planning cycle, unreachable objective, legitimate decomposition, and effect separation
  + [WPIO-020] measure deterministic exact joins before adding embeddings or learned routing and preserve the deterministic fallback

